  "slug": "cluster-topic-a230",
  "summary": "Four November 2026 preprints probe how environment shapes satellites, cluster-core SNe Ia, BCG dominance and radio-loud AGN incidence across cosmic time.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is environment as a probe of galaxy and stellar-population evolution, from the Local Group to z~3. HESTIA LCDM simulations are compared with Milky Way and Andromeda satellite pair statistics, which show an excess of close MW satellite pairs. ZTF photometry of likely cluster SNe Ia identifies 242 fast-declining events in cluster cores, supporting progenitor-age-driven stretch. A Gini-index analysis of 92 SPT and Planck clusters finds no evidence of BCG dominance evolving over 0<z<1, suggesting early BCG assembly. Euclid and LOFAR data show the LERG mass-slope flattening from about 2.5 locally to about 1.0 at higher redshift. The new element is quantitative, environment-resolved statistics, though the items address distinct systems and do not form a single analysis.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
